Fix an undefined `config` reference in the haybarn engine's
`extension_load.cpp` inside the `#ifdef WASM_LOADABLE_EXTENSIONS`
branch. Only manifests when the engine is compiled with
`WASM_LOADABLE_EXTENSIONS=1` (i.e. from this repo's `*_loadable`
build matrix entries) — native builds and non-loadable wasm builds
don't trip it because the dead branch is excluded by the preprocessor.

Function signature is `TryInitialLoad(DatabaseInstance &db, ...)`, so
the in-scope reference is `db.config`. Changing `&config` → `&db.config`
matches the rest of the function's existing pattern.

If/when the engine fork merges this fix upstream, the patch becomes a
"previously applied" no-op and can be deleted.

diff --git a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
--- a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
+++ b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
@@ -377,7 +377,7 @@
 		direct_load = false;
 		string extension_name = ApplyExtensionAlias(extension);
 #ifdef WASM_LOADABLE_EXTENSIONS
-		string url_template = ExtensionUrlTemplate(&config, "");
+		string url_template = ExtensionUrlTemplate(&db.config, "");
 		string url = ExtensionFinalizeUrlTemplate(url_template, extension_name);

 		char *str = (char *)EM_ASM_PTR(
